== __run_2
Rouh on Linux: one command. It checks this server, installs what is missing, and starts Rouh.

Checking this server
  ✓ Ubuntu 24.04.5 LTS, x86_64
  ✓ 4 processor cores
  ✓ 16 GB of memory
  ✓ 105 GB of free disk
  ✓ Python 3.12.3 for Rouh's updater
  ✓ Port 8420 is free (Rouh's page, on this machine only)
  ✓ Reaches rouh.land, ghcr.io and github.com

What happens now
  · Install Docker, from Docker's own packages (get.docker.com), with sudo
  · Get Rouh's updater (rouh-core) into /home/runner/rouh-core, at the commit rouh.land signed
  · Install the rouh command, and turn on the nightly update (03:00 to 05:00, after a backup)
  · Download and start Rouh: about 2 GB, about 5 minutes
  · Then set your Rouh up, here in this terminal: rouh setup
  Nothing of Rouh's listens beyond this machine. Uninstall any time: rouh uninstall

Installing what is missing

Checking what rouh.land hands out, before anything is installed
  ✓ rouh.land's release: signed with Rouh's key
  ✓ rouh.land's newest tested code: signed with Rouh's key (9493f679cb)
  Installing Docker (a few minutes)…
